meta {
  name: POST set charging current (max AC current)
  type: http
  seq: 35
}

put {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/charging/{{vin}}/set-charging-current
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "chargingCurrent": "REDUCED"
  }
}

docs {
  Sets the AC max charging current. Skoda exposes this as a two-value
  enum (MAXIMUM | REDUCED), NOT an integer amperage. No S-PIN required
  on Skoda mysmob — auth is bearer-only.

  Grounding:
    * endpoint — _private/research-archive/VAG_GROUP_ECOSYSTEM.md:260
      (mysmob POST command block, sibling of set-charge-limit).
    * enum     — the read side settings.maxChargingCurrent = "MAXIMUM"
      | "REDUCED" parsed by SkodaClient.get_charging_profiles
      (skoda.py). Same enum echoed back on write.

  Implementation: SkodaClient.command_update_charging_settings() in
  custom_components/vag_connect/cariad/api/skoda.py — dispatched by
  coordinator.async_update_charging_settings (brand-polymorphic, the
  same path SEAT/CUPRA uses via maxChargeCurrentAC on its own OLA
  endpoint).

  Backs the select.<vin>_skoda_charge_current_select entity
  (v2.15.10). Read state comes from the top-level max_charging_current
  field derived from the active charging profile.
}
